#: liminal-union/factions/liminal-union-braves.cfg:22
#: liminal-union/factions/liminal-union-heroes.cfg:22
msgid ""
"<bold><ref>text='The Liminal Union' dst='..race_maidencommand'</ref></bold> is a disciplined commonwealth fighting under an interlocking military doctrine. Strike at peak power with <bold>text='Three Golden Maxims'</bold>:\n"
"\n"
"1. <bold>text='March in Pairs'</bold>: Keep units adjacent to activate armor alloy traits automatically (Pyrite ranged focus, Kryonite damage Interlock, Arcanite Sunder). Resonance activates immediately upon stepping into formation.\n"
"2. <bold>text='Keep an Officer Close'</bold>: Officers and adjacent allied liminal units gain +10 percentage points of damage during Day or Night. Their alignment remains unchanged.\n"
"3. <bold>text='Strike at Twilight'</bold>: Attack fiercely at Dawn and Dusk (+25% power). By day and by night your troops fight at normal strength while lawful or chaotic foes are at their peak, so consolidate then.\n"
"\n"
"• <bold>text='Visual & Audio Feedback'</bold>: Color-coded breathing halos (Amber Pyrite, Cyan Kryonite, Purple Arcanite) and floating battle badges display tier status immediately without checking menus.\n"
"• <bold>text='Tactical Maneuvers'</bold>: Level 0 troops exert Zone of Control beside an officer; Pyrite troops glide from hills (+1 MP, Skirmisher); G9 Warforms overclock for an extra melee strike whose hits Stun; Mechatronics and Techtronics build warforms, Shieldguards call and rekindle Phoinixes.\n"
"• <bold>text='Arms'</bold>: Maidens shoot bodkin points and Pyrite fire; Marines hold the line with khopesh thrust and Kryonite cold; G9 Warforms brawl to slow and strike with Arcanite; Phoinixes strike arcane from afar and close with ember talons.\n"
"• <bold>text='Field Codex'</bold>: Right-click any unit anytime on the map, also during the opponent's turn, to review the Doctrine Codex."
msgstr ""

#. [multiplayer_side]: id=LIUN_heroes, type=LIUN_Maiden_Colonel
#: liminal-union/factions/liminal-union-heroes.cfg:21
msgid ""
"The <bold>text='Liminal Union: Heroes'</bold> (AoH) era features ♙lvl1 and ♙lvl2 recruits and ♕lvl3 leaders.\n"
""
msgstr ""

#: liminal-union/lua/codex.lua:18
msgid "Field Primer: Three Golden Maxims"
msgstr ""

#: liminal-union/lua/codex.lua:19
msgid ""
"To master the Liminal Union, keep three simple rules in mind:\n"
"\n"
"1. <b>March in Pairs:</b> Keep same-alloy troops adjacent to build Resonance. Its tier is based on the current formation and updates after every move and every fight. Poison disables Resonance; slow can reduce its tier.\n"
"\n"
"2. <b>Keep an Officer Close:</b> Conductors add 10 percentage points of damage for themselves and adjacent allied liminal units during Day or Night, the hours when lawful or chaotic enemies are strongest.\n"
"\n"
"3. <b>Strike at Twilight:</b> Liminal units deal 25% more damage at Dawn and Dusk.\n"
"\n"
"<b>Visual Feedback:</b>\n"
"• <i>Pulsing Halos:</i> Amber (Pyrite), Cyan (Kryonite), and Purple (Arcanite) halos and tier pips show Resonance status.\n"
"• <i>Battle Badges:</i> Floating notifications announce ZOC locks, Conductance, and Tier elevations without checking menus."
msgstr ""

#: liminal-union/lua/codex.lua:33
msgid "Resonance Pods & Armor Alloys"
msgstr ""

#: liminal-union/lua/codex.lua:34
msgid ""
"Resonance activates immediately when standing adjacent to allies with matching armor alloys. A pod of 2, 3 or 4+ units reaches Tier 1, 2 or 3; each tier grants +5% blade, pierce and impact resistance.\n"
"\n"
"• <b>Pyrite (Maidens):</b> <b>Focus</b>: +5% chance to hit per tier with ranged attacks on offense, +10% more beside a Hunterkiller Squad Anchor; a bow's own accuracy and Focus together never exceed +20%. Tier 3 adds +10% Fire and Arcane resistance.\n"
"• <b>Kryonite (Marines):</b> <b>Bulwark</b>: enemies lose 5% (Tier 1) or 10% (Tier 2+) chance to hit this unit in melee; a weapon's own parry and Bulwark together never exceed 15%. Tier 3 adds first strike on defense and +10% Cold and Arcane resistance. <b>Interlock</b> passes up to 30% of a normal hit to adjacent Kryonite allies; none falls below 1 HP. Magical and marksman strikes are not shared.\n"
"• <b>Arcanite (G9 Warforms, Techtronics):</b> <b>Sunder</b>: +1 melee damage per tier on offense, +1 more beside a Techtronic Squad Anchor, at most +3. Tier 3 adds +20% Fire and Cold resistance.\n"
"\n"
"<i>Poison disables resonance; slow can lower its tier.</i>"
msgstr ""

#: liminal-union/lua/codex.lua:44
msgid "Formation Zone of Control"
msgstr ""

#: liminal-union/lua/codex.lua:45
msgid ""
"Standard level 0 troops in Wesnoth exert no Zone of Control (ZOC).\n"
"\n"
"Liminal Union level 0 units (Marine/Maiden Privates, G9 AI, Ensigns) <b>exert full Zone of Control</b> while an allied officer (Ensign, Cornet, Captain or Colonel) stands adjacent and is not poisoned. Poison on the unit itself also removes it.\n"
"\n"
"Keep officers beside your conscripts to hold chokepoints, protect wounded comrades and deny cavalry breakthroughs; an officer who falls or moves away leaves the line open."
msgstr ""

#: liminal-union/lua/codex.lua:53
msgid "Conductance & Alignment"
msgstr ""

#: liminal-union/lua/codex.lua:54
msgid ""
"Liminal Union troops are liminal: they deal <b>+25% damage at Dawn and Dusk</b> and fight at normal strength by Day and by Night. They suffer no day or night penalty, but lawful enemies gain +25% by Day and chaotic enemies +25% at Night, so those hours favour the opponent.\n"
"\n"
"All Command units (Ensigns, Cornets, Captains, Colonels) radiate a <b>Conductance Aura</b> (pulsing ground halo). The officer and adjacent allied liminal units gain +10 percentage points of damage:\n"
"• <b>Day:</b> +10% instead of 0%.\n"
"• <b>Night:</b> +10% instead of 0%.\n"
"• <b>Dawn/Dusk:</b> no extra bonus; the twilight +25% applies.\n"
"\n"
"<i>Officers narrow the gap to lawful and chaotic enemies during their strong hours; they change no one's alignment.</i>"
msgstr ""

#: liminal-union/lua/codex.lua:65
msgid "Unit Stages (level·stage)"
msgstr ""

#: liminal-union/lua/codex.lua:66
msgid ""
"Liminal Union unit names end in <b>(level·stage)</b>. <b>(0·1)</b> is a level 0 unit in its second doctrine stage; <b>(1·0)</b> is a fresh level 1 unit.\n"
"\n"
"• Filling the experience bar moves a unit to its next doctrine stage of the same level. The new stage unlocks a weapon, an ability or more hit points, but it heals only 2 HP and keeps poison and slow.\n"
"• At the last stage of a level, the next advancement is a full level-up, which heals as usual and may offer a choice of lines.\n"
"• The unit description lists what each stage unlocks."
msgstr ""

#: liminal-union/lua/codex.lua:74
msgid "Tactical Maneuvers"
msgstr ""

#: liminal-union/lua/codex.lua:75
msgid ""
"<i>Expert doctrine. Right-click actions appear in the context menu only while a unit can use them right now.</i>\n"
"\n"
"• <b>Marine Salt-Grounding Pylum (Right-Click):</b> Right-click an ungrounded Kryonite Marine (Sergeant or higher; not Privates or Officers) to deploy their conductive pylon stake. Grants adjacent allies +20% elemental warding, grounds adjacent enemies' fire, cold and arcane attacks (max 50% CTH), and reduces enemy elemental damage by 20%. Costs: 0 MP and +20% melee Blade/Impact vulnerability. Lasts through the following enemy turn; redeploy it on your next turn.\n"
"• <b>G9 Overclock (Right-Click):</b> Right-click a G9 Warform with more than 4 HP and an attack left to trigger emergency protocol bypass: +1 melee strike for this turn, and every melee hit <b>stuns</b> a level 1+ enemy, which loses its zone of control until its own side's next turn begins. At turn end, the golem suffers up to 3 HP core thermal stress and cannot die from it.\n"
"• <b>Maiden Wingsuit Glide (Passive):</b> Any Pyrite-armored unit beginning its turn on elevated terrain (Hills or Mountains) deploys thermal wingsuits, gaining <b>+1 MP and Skirmisher</b> for that turn!\n"
"• <b>Portal Warden (Passive):</b> A Shieldguard that stood still for a full turn with a Phoinix beside it opens its portable Arcanite portal, charged by mana crystals. Marines other than leaders may travel one way from your villages to free hexes beside it, arriving with no moves and no attack that turn. The portal closes when the Shieldguard moves.\n"
"• <b>Field Works (Right-Click):</b> Mechatronics and Techtronics standing on a village, castle or keep spend one aimergent-core and gold to build a G8 Simulacrum (10 gold) or a G9 AI (20 gold) on a free hex beside them. Shieldguards open an ember capsule (10 gold) to call a Phoinix, or kindle the ash of a fallen Phoinix for free. Each new unit of these lines carries 3 charges; the sidebar shows how many remain."
msgstr ""

